<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kadesh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1274 BCE</span> · Also known as Kadesh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kadesh was fought in 1274 BCE near Kadesh on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontes-river">Orontes River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> between the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> and the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a>. It is one of the best-documented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> battles of antiquity and ended without a decisive result, despite Egyptian claims of victory. It was followed later by a peace treaty between the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh.jpg" alt="Battle of Kadesh" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypt_Abou_Simbel6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
